[2026-02-01T21:36:41.976Z] [STDOUT] {"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_018WpdvWcPb6AULLcemQwCZ3","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→# Research Explorer\n     2→\n     3→## What This Is\n     4→\n     5→A research initiation and exploration platform. Users discover newsworthy topics from 10 data sources (Twitter, BBC, Reuters, etc.), review and initiate deep research on selected topics with a single click, and track research progress in real-time. The platform combines LLM-powered topic discovery with automated research generation.\n     6→\n     7→## Core Value\n     8→\n     9→Enable users to efficiently discover, prioritize, and initiate research on newsworthy topics from diverse data sources.\n    10→\n    11→## Current State (v2.0 Shipped)\n    12→\n    13→**Shipped:** 2026-02-01\n    14→**Codebase:** 73,187 lines TypeScript\n    15→\n    16→**Delivered:**\n    17→- `/initiate` page with 10-column topic dashboard\n    18→- LLM-powered topic discovery with Google Search grounding\n    19→- One-click research initiation with source-based template selection\n    20→- Real-time status polling (5-second interval)\n    21→- Queue dashboard showing all active research\n    22→- View Results for completed topics, Retry for failed\n    23→\n    24→**Tech Stack:**\n    25→- Next.js 16 + React 19 + Tailwind CSS 4\n    26→- Supabase PostgreSQL (data_sources, research_topics tables)\n    27→- Gemini API with structured output for discovery\n    28→- Python actor on Cloud Run for research generation\n    29→- TanStack Virtual for 60fps list rendering\n    30→\n    31→## Requirements\n    32→\n    33→### Validated (v2.0)\n    34→\n    35→- ✓ 10-column grid layout with horizontal scroll — v2.0\n    36→- ✓ Virtualized lists handle 100+ items at 60fps — v2.0\n    37→- ✓ TopicCard with status indicators (WCAG compliant) — v2.0\n    38→- ✓ LLM discovery with Google Search grounding — v2.0\n    39→- ✓ URL validation (HEAD request health check) — v2.0\n    40→- ✓ Rate limiting (max 3 concurrent discovery requests) — v2.0\n    41→- ✓ Research initiation returns HTTP 202 with session ID — v2.0\n    42→- ✓ Template selected based on source — v2.0\n    43→- ✓ Status polling every 5 seconds — v2.0\n    44→- ✓ Queue dashboard shows all pending/active research — v2.0\n    45→- ✓ View Results opens research session — v2.0\n    46→- ✓ Retry re-initiates failed research — v2.0\n    47→\n    48→### Validated (v1.0)\n    49→\n    50→- ✓ Research sessions stored in Supabase with template types, findings, sources\n    51→- ✓ Python actor generates research with Gemini + web search grounding\n    52→- ✓ Theme switcher with persistence (Radar, Swiss, Organic)\n    53→- ✓ Semantic CSS variable system (~35 variables)\n    54→\n    55→### Active (v3+ Candidates)\n    56→\n    57→**Differentiators:**\n    58→- [ ] Signal badges (breaking/trending/controversial) on topic cards\n    59→- [ ] Density toggle (comfortable vs compact mode)\n    60→- [ ] Column collapse/expand\n    61→- [ ] Quick preview on hover\n    62→- [ ] Research history context (\"Researched 3 days ago\")\n    63→- [ ] Bulk selection with \"Research all selected\"\n    64→- [ ] Keyboard shortcuts (j/k navigation, r to research)\n    65→\n    66→**Advanced:**\n    67→- [ ] AI-powered topic deduplication across sources\n    68→- [ ] Topic clustering by theme (Politics, Tech, Markets)\n    69→- [ ] Batch scheduling (\"Research all at 6 PM\")\n    70→- [ ] Priority scoring via LLM\n    71→\n    72→**Deferred from v1:**\n    73→- [ ] Navigation shell (template selector, breadcrumb)\n    74→- [ ] Topic map visualization\n    75→- [ ] Transitions and animations\n    76→\n    77→### Out of Scope\n    78→\n    79→- Search functionality — discovery-first approach\n    80→- User authentication/multi-tenant — single user for now\n    81→- Mobile-first design — desktop primary\n    82→- Automated/scheduled discovery — on-demand only\n    83→- Topic editing — only delete and research actions\n    84→\n    85→## Context\n    86→\n    87→**Database Schema:**\n    88→- `data_sources` — 10 source definitions (Twitter, BBC, etc.)\n    89→- `research_topics` — Topics with status, session_id link\n    90→- `research_sessions` — Sessions with template_type, findings, sources\n    91→\n    92→**API Routes:**\n    93→- `POST /api/topics/discover` — LLM discovery with rate limiting\n    94→- `POST /api/topics/{id}/research` — Initiate research (202 response)\n    95→- `GET /api/topics/status` — Batch status for polling\n    96→\n    97→## Constraints\n    98→\n    99→- **Performance**: 10 lists visible at 60fps (virtualization required)\n   100→- **Data compatibility**: Extend Supabase schema, don't break existing tables\n   101→- **Theme**: Swiss theme only for v2 (other themes available but not focus)\n   102→- **Actor integration**: Triggers existing Python research actor\n   103→\n   104→## Key Decisions\n   105→\n   106→| Decision | Rationale | Outcome |\n   107→|----------|-----------|---------|\n   108→| Pivot from v1 explorer to v2 initiation | User priority shifted to research initiation workflow | ✓ Good |\n   109→| 10-column layout for source lists | Maximize information density, minimize scrolling | ✓ Good |\n   110→| Swiss theme only for v2 | Focus on functionality first, visual variety later | ✓ Good |\n   111→| LLM discovery on-demand | Avoid background processing complexity | ✓ Good |\n   112→| Soft delete for topics | Preserve data for audit, allow recovery | ✓ Good |\n   113→| useFlushSync: false for TanStack Virtual | React 19 compatibility | ✓ Good |\n   114→| HEAD request URL validation | 34% hallucination rate from LLM | ✓ Good |\n   115→| Semaphore for rate limiting | Fast-fail 429 responses | ✓ Good |\n   116→| Conditional DB update for idempotency | Race condition prevention | ✓ Good |\n   117→| Visibility API for polling | Pause on hidden tabs | ✓ Good |\n   118→\n   119→---\n   120→*Last updated: 2026-02-01 after v2.0 milestone completion*\n   121→\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"64f38134-a29f-4fa9-a1bc-982d6533f758","uuid":"9bb753ac-1a70-4b26-b6b7-24d96f8a8f47","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"C:\\Users\\mkdol\\dolla\\res\\.planning\\PROJECT.md","content":"# Research Explorer\n\n## What This Is\n\nA research initiation and exploration platform. Users discover newsworthy topics from 10 data sources (Twitter, BBC, Reuters, etc.), review and initiate deep research on selected topics with a single click, and track research progress in real-time. The platform combines LLM-powered topic discovery with automated research generation.\n\n## Core Value\n\nEnable users to efficiently discover, prioritize, and initiate research on newsworthy topics from diverse data sources.\n\n## Current State (v2.0 Shipped)\n\n**Shipped:** 2026-02-01\n**Codebase:** 73,187 lines TypeScript\n\n**Delivered:**\n- `/initiate` page with 10-column topic dashboard\n- LLM-powered topic discovery with Google Search grounding\n- One-click research initiation with source-based template selection\n- Real-time status polling (5-second interval)\n- Queue dashboard showing all active research\n- View Results for completed topics, Retry for failed\n\n**Tech Stack:**\n- Next.js 16 + React 19 + Tailwind CSS 4\n- Supabase PostgreSQL (data_sources, research_topics tables)\n- Gemini API with structured output for discovery\n- Python actor on Cloud Run for research generation\n- TanStack Virtual for 60fps list rendering\n\n## Requirements\n\n### Validated (v2.0)\n\n- ✓ 10-column grid layout with horizontal scroll — v2.0\n- ✓ Virtualized lists handle 100+ items at 60fps — v2.0\n- ✓ TopicCard with status indicators (WCAG compliant) — v2.0\n- ✓ LLM discovery with Google Search grounding — v2.0\n- ✓ URL validation (HEAD request health check) — v2.0\n- ✓ Rate limiting (max 3 concurrent discovery requests) — v2.0\n- ✓ Research initiation returns HTTP 202 with session ID — v2.0\n- ✓ Template selected based on source — v2.0\n- ✓ Status polling every 5 seconds — v2.0\n- ✓ Queue dashboard shows all pending/active research — v2.0\n- ✓ View Results opens research session — v2.0\n- ✓ Retry re-initiates failed research — v2.0\n\n### Validated (v1.0)\n\n- ✓ Research sessions stored in Supabase with template types, findings, sources\n- ✓ Python actor generates research with Gemini + web search grounding\n- ✓ Theme switcher with persistence (Radar, Swiss, Organic)\n- ✓ Semantic CSS variable system (~35 variables)\n\n### Active (v3+ Candidates)\n\n**Differentiators:**\n- [ ] Signal badges (breaking/trending/controversial) on topic cards\n- [ ] Density toggle (comfortable vs compact mode)\n- [ ] Column collapse/expand\n- [ ] Quick preview on hover\n- [ ] Research history context (\"Researched 3 days ago\")\n- [ ] Bulk selection with \"Research all selected\"\n- [ ] Keyboard shortcuts (j/k navigation, r to research)\n\n**Advanced:**\n- [ ] AI-powered topic deduplication across sources\n- [ ] Topic clustering by theme (Politics, Tech, Markets)\n- [ ] Batch scheduling (\"Research all at 6 PM\")\n- [ ] Priority scoring via LLM\n\n**Deferred from v1:**\n- [ ] Navigation shell (template selector, breadcrumb)\n- [ ] Topic map visualization\n- [ ] Transitions and animations\n\n### Out of Scope\n\n- Search functionality — discovery-first approach\n- User authentication/multi-tenant — single user for now\n- Mobile-first design — desktop primary\n- Automated/scheduled discovery — on-demand only\n- Topic editing — only delete and research actions\n\n## Context\n\n**Database Schema:**\n- `data_sources` — 10 source definitions (Twitter, BBC, etc.)\n- `research_topics` — Topics with status, session_id link\n- `research_sessions` — Sessions with template_type, findings, sources\n\n**API Routes:**\n- `POST /api/topics/discover` — LLM discovery with rate limiting\n- `POST /api/topics/{id}/research` — Initiate research (202 response)\n- `GET /api/topics/status` — Batch status for polling\n\n## Constraints\n\n- **Performance**: 10 lists visible at 60fps (virtualization required)\n- **Data compatibility**: Extend Supabase schema, don't break existing tables\n- **Theme**: Swiss theme only for v2 (other themes available but not focus)\n- **Actor integration**: Triggers existing Python research actor\n\n## Key Decisions\n\n| Decision | Rationale | Outcome |\n|----------|-----------|---------|\n| Pivot from v1 explorer to v2 initiation | User priority shifted to research initiation workflow | ✓ Good |\n| 10-column layout for source lists | Maximize information density, minimize scrolling | ✓ Good |\n| Swiss theme only for v2 | Focus on functionality first, visual variety later | ✓ Good |\n| LLM discovery on-demand | Avoid background processing complexity | ✓ Good |\n| Soft delete for topics | Preserve data for audit, allow recovery | ✓ Good |\n| useFlushSync: false for TanStack Virtual | React 19 compatibility | ✓ Good |\n| HEAD request URL validation | 34% hallucination rate from LLM | ✓ Good |\n| Semaphore for rate limiting | Fast-fail 429 responses | ✓ Good |\n| Conditional DB update for idempotency | Race condition prevention | ✓ Good |\n| Visibility API for polling | Pause on hidden tabs | ✓ Good |\n\n---\n*Last updated: 2026-02-01 after v2.0 milestone completion*\n","numLines":121,"startLine":1,"totalLines":121}}}
